1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,163
Nobody crashed.

2
00:00:01,163 --> 00:00:02,069
Nobody merged.

3
00:00:02,069 --> 00:00:03,145
So why did all

4
00:00:03,145 --> 00:00:04,674
this traffic just stop?

5
00:00:05,233 --> 00:00:06,356
Get to the front,

6
00:00:06,356 --> 00:00:07,908
and there's nothing there.

7
00:00:07,908 --> 00:00:08,657
No accident.

8
00:00:08,657 --> 00:00:09,405
No roadwork.

9
00:00:09,967 --> 00:00:11,573
In a 2008 study,

10
00:00:11,573 --> 00:00:13,903
researchers in Japan put

11
00:00:13,903 --> 00:00:15,268
22 cars on a

12
00:00:15,268 --> 00:00:17,437
230-metre circular track,

13
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,379
and asked every driver

14
00:00:19,379 --> 00:00:20,554
to cruise at about

15
00:00:20,554 --> 00:00:21,882
30 kilometres an hour.

16
00:00:22,433 --> 00:00:23,813
The smooth flow didn't

17
00:00:23,813 --> 00:00:24,132
last.

18
00:00:24,132 --> 00:00:25,512
When one driver eases

19
00:00:25,512 --> 00:00:26,362
off a little,

20
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:28,195
the driver behind reacts

21
00:00:28,195 --> 00:00:29,177
a moment late and

22
00:00:29,177 --> 00:00:30,382
brakes a little harder.

23
00:00:30,382 --> 00:00:31,587
The next driver brakes

24
00:00:31,587 --> 00:00:32,257
harder still.

25
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,442
Those tiny delays grow

26
00:00:34,442 --> 00:00:36,024
into a stop-and-go wave

27
00:00:36,024 --> 00:00:37,605
that travels backwards,

28
00:00:37,605 --> 00:00:39,004
against the traffic.

29
00:00:39,567 --> 00:00:40,642
On real highways,

30
00:00:40,642 --> 00:00:42,041
waves like this drift

31
00:00:42,041 --> 00:00:43,815
backwards at roughly fifteen

32
00:00:43,815 --> 00:00:45,321
to twenty kilometres an

33
00:00:45,321 --> 00:00:45,644
hour.

34
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:47,507
Later experiments found

35
00:00:47,507 --> 00:00:48,912
a single smoothly driven

36
00:00:48,912 --> 00:00:50,219
car could dampen these

37
00:00:50,219 --> 00:00:50,558
waves.

38
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:52,111
So leave a little

39
00:00:52,111 --> 00:00:52,754
extra space.

40
00:00:52,754 --> 00:00:53,719
You might be the

41
00:00:53,719 --> 00:00:54,776
one who smooths it

42
00:00:54,776 --> 00:00:55,076
out.
